OL,3,ANew Zealand opposition leader says
OL,4,Aparties will need to 'work together' as
OL,5,Avote count shows tight race
OL,6,
OL,7,FMeanwhile, the centrist Opportunity
OL,8,FParty crosses the 5% threshold to enter
OL,9,Fparliament for the first time as the
OL,10,Fmajor parties see historically low
OL,11,Fvotes
OL,13,FNew Zealand's voting system - mixed
OL,14,Fmember proportional - means most
OL,15,Fgovernments are coalitions
OL,17,FSymone, 28, says most of her friends
OL,18,Fhave left New Zealand or are
OL,19,Fconsidering leaving. She tells our
OL,20,Freporter in Wellington: "I think we're
OL,21,Fall tired... that's one of the reasons
OL,22,FI want change"
OL,23,APub: 07-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
